<title>UK: Securicor up on telephone bid talk.</title>
<headline>Securicor up on telephone bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK security group Securicor Plc were lifted on Wednesday by talk the government will allow British Telecom to buy Securicor's stake in mobile 'phone operator Cellnet. Securicor shares were up 5-1/2p or two percent at 270p by 1443 GMT. Just over 950,000 shares had changed hands. The overall market was up 0.57 percent.</p>
<p>Dealers said a report in the Daily Mail newspaper relaying the market talk had intensified interest in the stock.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
